card.statement:
Let $A=\TGWA{R}{\si}{t}{\mu}$ be a $\K$-finitistic TGW algebra where $(R,\si,t)$ is $\mu$-consistent. Let $p_{ij}$ be the minimal polynomials defined above.

[(a)]

- Define the matrix $C_A=(a_{ij})$ with integer entries as follows:

\begin{equation}
a_{ij}=
\begin{cases}
2,&i=j,\\
1-\deg p_{ij},&i\neq j.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

Then $C_A$ is a generalized Cartan matrix.

- Assume $t_i$ is regular in $R$ for all $i$. Writing

\[p_{ij}(x)=x^{m_{ij}}+\la_{ij}^{(1)}x^{m_{ij}-1}+\cdots+\la_{ij}^{(m_{ij})},\]

where all $\la_{ij}^{(k)}\in\K$, the following identities hold in $A$, for any $i\neq j$:

\begin{equation}
X_i^{m_{ij}}X_j+\la_{ij}^{(1)}\mu_{ij}^{-1} X_i^{m_{ij}-1}X_jX_i+
\cdots + \la_{ij}^{(m_{ij})} \mu_{ij}^{-m_{ij}}X_jX_i^{m_{ij}}=0
\end{equation}

and

\begin{equation}
Y_jY_i^{m_{ij}}+\la_{ij}^{(1)}\mu_{ji}^{-1} Y_iY_jY_i^{m_{ij}-1}+
\cdots + \la_{ij}^{(m_{ij})} \mu_{ji}^{-m_{ij}}Y_i^{m_{ij}}Y_j=0.
\end{equation}

Moreover, for any $i\neq j$ and $m<m_{ij}$, the sets $\{X_i^{m-k}X_jX_i^k\}_{k=0}^m$ and $\{Y_i^{m-k}Y_jY_i^k\}_{k=0}^m$ are linearly independent in $A$ over $\K$.
